                                    <span class="meter-fill" style="--n: 2"></span>
                                </span>
                            </dd>
                        </div>
                    </dl>
                    <p class="evidence">
                        <b>Evidence:</b> eight route groups mounted on one Express app, with
                        controllers delegating every query to a model module.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="card" data-reveal>
                    <h3>MySQL &amp; SQL</h3>
                    <p>
                        Designing the tables before writing the queries. Relations, joins, and
                        parameterised statements everywhere, because building the string yourself is
                        how you end up with a security problem.
                    </p>
                    <dl>
                        <div class="skill-row">
                            <dt>Schema design</dt>
                            <dd class="is-core">
                                <span>Foundational+</span>
                                <span class="meter" role="img" aria-label="Foundational plus, three of five">
                                    <span class="meter-fill" style="--n: 3"></span>
                                </span>
                            </dd>
                        </div>
                        <div class="skill-row">
                            <dt>Joins</dt>
                            <dd>
                                <span>Foundational</span>
